/target
# the CI test lane's own CARGO_TARGET_DIR (.woodpecker/ci.yaml): a build dir
# like /target; untracked it makes the publish step's tree probe read dirty.
/target-ci
/.claude/worktrees
# per-run history: CI artifacts carry it; only the current table + latest.json are tracked
/crates/perfsuite/results/20*.json
/.claude/agent-memory
/.claude/settings.local.json
/result
# live drawer: the daemon writes this when meridian-rs is a bound workspace
/.meridian/
# the registry's currency sentinel (crates/registry/src/feed.rs), written into
# ANY drawer a daemon binds — including the parity corpora's own `.meridian/`,
# which the rule above never sees. `**/` is load-bearing: a pattern with a
# separator anywhere but the end is anchored to this file's own directory, so
# the bare `.meridian/cookie` matches the root drawer and nothing under
# `crates/`. Named rather than ignoring the nested drawer: those drawers carry
# TRACKED fixtures (`stable-read.probe`) and the parity pack is a byte-exact
# copy of an upstream corpus that must not be edited around. A local test run
# otherwise puts these into a commit.
# Verify, do not assume: `git check-ignore -v <a nested cookie path>`.
**/.meridian/cookie
# seat scratch: lives beside the worktree, never in the tree
.scratch/
/.scratch-*.yaml
